      "description": "Quiet route links with a fine current-route marker.",
      "html": "<nav class=\"ds-nav\" aria-label=\"Example navigation\"><a href=\"#work\" aria-current=\"page\">Work</a><a href=\"#journal\">Journal</a><a href=\"#about\">About</a></nav>",
      "css": ".ds-nav{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:28px;color:var(--ink,#30291f);font:400 16px/1.5 'DM Sans',sans-serif}.ds-nav a{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;min-height:44px;padding:9px 0;text-decoration:none;color:inherit}.ds-nav a:hover,.ds-nav a[aria-current=page]{color:#805c29}.ds-nav a[aria-current=page]{box-shadow:0 1px 0 #a27c46}.ds-nav a:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #9a672a;outline-offset:5px}@media(max-width:760px){.ds-nav{flex-direction:column;align-items:stretch;gap:8px}.ds-nav a{font-size:18px;padding:12px 0}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Work Tags",
      "kind": "chip",
      "refersTo": "tag",
      "description": "Noninteractive category and content labels.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-tags\"><span>Literature</span><span>Art</span><span>Media</span></div>",
      "css": ".ds-tags{display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap}.ds-tags span{color:#6b5b44;background:#eee7da;padding:6px 10px;border-radius:4px;font:400 12px 'DM Sans',sans-serif}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Editorial Work Card",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "artwork",
      "description": "Open article structure with modest image corners and no panel shadow. Preview omits external artwork.",
      "html": "<article class=\"ds-card\"><a class=\"ds-image\" href=\"#project\" aria-label=\"View project\"><svg class=\"ds-art\" viewBox=\"0 0 360 190\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path fill=\"#e8dfcf\" d=\"M0 0h360v190H0z\"/></svg><span class=\"ds-card-arrow\"><svg width=\"23\" height=\"23\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M7 17 17 7M7 7h10v10\"/></svg></span></a><div class=\"ds-title\"><h3><a href=\"#project\">Selected work</a></h3><span>Art</span></div><p>Stories, images, and experiences, given a considered form.</p></article>",
      "css": ".ds-card{min-width:0;color:var(--ink,#30291f);font-family:'DM Sans',sans-serif}.ds-image{display:block;position:relative;overflow:hidden;aspect-ratio:1.9;background:#e7ded0;border-radius:6px}.ds-art{height:100%;width:100%;object-fit:cover;transition:transform .7s cubic-bezier(.2,.8,.2,1)}.ds-image:hover .ds-art{transform:scale(1.035)}.ds-card-arrow{background:var(--paper,#faf7f0);color:var(--ink,#30291f);border-radius:50%;position:absolute;right:16px;bottom:16px;height:40px;width:40px;display:grid;place-items:center}.ds-title{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:baseline;gap:16px;padding:20px 0 10px}.ds-title h3{font:500 2.3rem/1.04 'Cormorant Garamond',Georgia,serif;letter-spacing:-.025em;margin:0}.ds-title a{color:inherit;text-decoration:none}.ds-title a:hover{color:#805c29}.ds-title>span{color:var(--muted,#746957);font-size:13px}.ds-card>p{color:#675c4c;font-size:15px;max-width:70ch;line-height:1.75;margin:0}.ds-card a:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #9a672a;outline-offset:5px}@media(max-width:760px){.ds-image{aspect-ratio:1.65}.ds-title{padding-top:16px}.ds-title h3{font-size:2.2rem}}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.ds-art{transition-duration:.01ms!important}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Chapter Arrow",
      "kind": "button",
      "refersTo": "chapter-arrow",
      "description": "Persistent presentation navigation with a round rule and explicit boundary state.",
      "html": "<button class=\"ds-chapter-arrow\" aria-label=\"Next chapter\"><svg width=\"19\" height=\"19\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14m-6-6 6 6-6 6\"/></svg></button>",
      "css": ".ds-chapter-arrow{min-width:44px;min-height:44px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;border:1px solid #e3e5df;border-radius:50%;background:#fff;color:#272925;cursor:pointer;transition:background .15s}.ds-chapter-arrow:hover{background:#f5f5f1}.ds-chapter-arrow:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #9a672a;outline-offset:5px}.ds-chapter-arrow:disabled{opacity:.35;cursor:default}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.ds-chapter-arrow{transition-duration:.01ms!important}}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Veil of Light with Jade Horizon",
    "overview": "Waisery carries the confirmed Chinese celestial direction: elegant, dignified, grand, and striking. White-jade architecture, cloud seas, pale-gold light, fine openwork, translucent layers, and an anonymous dark figure establish the imagery. The figure is an atmospheric illustration, not a portrait of the portfolio owner. Spacious serif headlines and restrained functional text keep the work legible within that world. All interface copy and project documentation use English.\n\nThe implemented home is a pure-white, five-chapter presentation with deliberate keyframed changes between Opening, Work, About, Journal, and Contact. Inner routes retain the warm ivory, gold, and ink system for browsing, reading, forms, and management. The home composition is a route-specific expression; its viewport presentation is not a requirement for other screens.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Spacious typography with a clear distinction between literary display and functional text.",
      "Celestial artwork balanced by quiet white or ivory surfaces.",
      "Ink actions, fine warm rules, modest corners, and restrained motion.",
      "Responsive reading space with explicit keyboard, focus, status, and reduced-motion behavior."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Scoped Paper Rule",
        "body": "Pure white belongs to the homepage presentation and its header; inner routes keep warm paper unless an existing component explicitly defines another surface.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Two Voices Rule",
        "body": "Use Cormorant Garamond for expressive headings and literary passages; use DM Sans for controls and functional information.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Quiet Surface Rule",
        "body": "Keep ordinary content surfaces flat and express separation through space, rules, and the existing paper tones.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do preserve the scoped white homepage and warm ivory inner-route distinction.",
      "Do keep serif display and literary text paired with sans-serif functional copy.",
      "Do preserve the celestial artwork's anonymous figure, luminous architecture, and restrained gold character.",
      "Do keep overflow content readable, focus visible, scene announcements available, and native media controls independent.",
      "Do use the existing responsive grids and reduced-motion behavior when extending a component."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't apply the homepage's viewport presentation to reading or management routes without an explicit new design decision.",
      "Don't use the illustrated figure as the portfolio owner's portrait.",
      "Don't replace ordinary flat content surfaces with decorative elevation or remove the existing focus outlines.",
      "Don't treat generated sidecar tonal ramps as additional production color tokens."
    ]
  }
}
